{"id":"dag","ord":"a0","title":"DAG","desc":"Workflow TEMPLATES — the pipeline a lane walks, defined ONCE as a subtree.\n\n- Each step is a `todo` node; dependencies are `after` edges.\n- The app draws blocked-vs-ready, so the template is its own diagram.\n- `set_doing` refusing on a blocked node makes the order a refusal rather than a discipline.\n- **LAW:** never mark anything here.\n  - Dispatch CLONES a template under a new lane node in lanes.olai (real copies via `add_node`, one call with `children`).\n  - Then rewrites the `after` edges onto the clone's ids with `set_after`.\n  - Capture children cannot carry edges yet — the one wrinkle this prototype surfaced.\n- **Step ids:** `dag-<template>-<step>`; a clone keeps the `<step>` suffixes under a `lane-<task>-` prefix, so mark-flipping needs no search.\n- **Edge rule** the template must encode: a step that MUTATES the worktree sits `after` every step that READS it — readers fan out, writers wait.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T18:59:50-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr","parent":"dag","ord":"a0","title":"pr — implement through merge","desc":"The default pipeline for a dispatched PR lane. Facts the clone carries as properties: `agent`/`repo`/`item` on the lane node, `terminal` on implement, `pr` on the step that opened it.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-implement","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a0","title":"implement + open PR","todo":true,"desc":"Dispatch IS `set_doing` here. The clone's copy carries `terminal` as a property; `pr-url` lands when the PR opens.\n\nTHE STAGE'S LAW (graduated from instructions.md — ir-pipeline-prose, 2026-08-25):\n- The author opens the PR with its initial implementation and NEVER merges it.\n- The author's bar at report time is the LOCAL suites — typecheck, unit, the touched features, run serially and light. NEVER full CI: CI is the orchestrator's, once, at the ci step (whose desc carries the 2026-08-25 ruling and its provenance).\n- The report ends at the PR URL @ head, and the author STOPS — no commissioning reviews, no merging, no board writes, kill by PID only.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:16-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-refactor","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1","title":"refactor passes","todo":true,"desc":"Only for a non-trivial, non-test-only code change — otherwise SKIPPED.\n\n- The author refactors its own PR, pushing each step as an isolated commit.\n- **Method:**\n  - architecture-first-principles (kolu's skill: .agents/skills/architecture-first-principles/SKILL.md)\n  - hickey (srid/agency .apm/skills/hickey) and lowy (.apm/skills/lowy) *together*, using human intuition so as to keep architecture simple\n  - /simplify when the author is Claude\n- These are method, not ordered sub-steps — one step here, deliberately.","after":["dag-pr-implement"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:21-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge-master","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a4","title":"merge latest master into the PR","todo":true,"desc":"A MERGE COMMIT, never a rebase.\n\n- **Ruled:** 2026-08-15 — faster, and history stays put.\n- Per CLAUDE.md this step runs ONLY when the PR has conflicts or CI needs code from master — otherwise it is SKIPPED, same pattern as the deferral gate.\n- **Writer:** sits after both reviews because it mutates the worktree they read.\n  - The 2026-08-15 rebase-under-live-reviewers incident is why this edge exists.\n- CONFLICT HYGIENE IS CONTINUOUS (graduated, ir-pipeline-prose 2026-08-25): the orchestrator checks the PR still merges cleanly into master when the author finishes and again after review fixes — conflicts fixed immediately, never discovered at merge time.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:43-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-address","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a5","title":"address findings","todo":true,"desc":"The author addresses the folded findings, given the PR comment link. No deferrals — the gate below owns the law; a finding that genuinely cannot be addressed here is a STOP-AND-ASK in the author's terminal, never a note in the PR.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:48-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-ci","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a6","title":"CI green at head","todo":true,"desc":"CI runs ONCE per PR in the happy path, after the review round — and THE ORCHESTRATOR RUNS IT, never the author (ruled 2026-08-25, provenance: the typed-properties author reported `just check`-local as \"CI green\" — the author grades its own homework; the runner must have no stake. Authors' reports end at \"head X ready\"). CI = odu per its SKILL.md read in FULL (CLAUDE.md's definition); venue rulings live on supervision-watcher's `odu-venue` props.\n\nGREEN IS EXPLICIT (the old green-ci footnote, graduated): never judge from the check rollup — it lists only checks that already reported, so a required check that hasn't started looks like success. `gh pr checks <n> --required` must show an explicit pass on every required check, or mergeStateStatus == CLEAN.\n\nA re-verdict round that changes code re-runs CI at the new head; that run is the price of the finding.","after":["dag-pr-merge-master","dag-pr-address"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:55-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-evidence","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a7","title":"evidence verified","todo":true,"desc":"The author produces a screenshot (or video) proving the change working; the ORCHESTRATOR frame-verifies it before the PR is fielded to the human. Upload recipes (the GitHub user-attachments endpoint, mp4 transcode) live in CLAUDE.md — where every worker agent already reads (ruled 2026-08-25, closing ir-evidence-recipe-reach).","after":["dag-pr-ci"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:59-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-deferrals","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a8","title":"deferrals ruled #human","todo":true,"desc":"HUMAN gate: a PR whose report carries deferrals merges only on the human's explicit word — each deferral becomes a roadmap node first. A report that says \"no deferrals\" in so many words skips this gate.\n\nTHE LAW (graduated from instructions.md — ir-pipeline-prose, 2026-08-25): a PR ships everything its roadmap item names and everything it spots in the code it touches — refactors of touched code, pre-existing hacks, review findings, nits. Diff size, noise, review burden, \"different shape\", \"wants its own PR\" are never reasons; neither is another repository's gate or a design question. What genuinely cannot be done in the PR is a STOP-AND-ASK in the author's terminal (what, why it cannot be done here, the options), and the orchestrator puts the question to the human before the PR moves (overnight autonomy excepted). A `## Deferrals` section saying anything but `No deferrals.` is not merge-ready, and \"filed as a follow-up\" counts as a deferral. The Inbox holds only what the human chooses to park.","after":["dag-pr-evidence"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:05:06-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a9","title":"merge","todo":true,"desc":"THE STAGE'S LAW (graduated from instructions.md — ir-pipeline-prose, 2026-08-25):\n\n- Approval opens a GATE, it does not skip the pipeline: whatever is still in flight finishes first — review posted, findings addressed, CI green at head (the ci step's explicit-pass bar). The merge-gate law (agents-root) stands: no merge without the human's explicit approval except pre-authorized auto gates.\n- Then SQUASH merge. Conflicts → the lane's author resolves them, then retry.\n- Multiple approvals merge in the order that minimizes conflict-resolution work.\n- Before fielding a PR for approval: read the author's FINAL message in its terminal (kolu snapshot). Anything left \"for you\" is a STOP-AND-ASK, not a note — the PR waits on the human's answer (overnight autonomy excepted).\n- Never file issues or take any action on another repo without the human's ratification. \"Recorded\" in prose is not tracked; only a URL or a roadmap entry is.","after":["dag-pr-deferrals"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:05:12-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-retire","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"aA","title":"retire terminals","todo":true,"desc":"Kill EVERY terminal the lane spawned — the author too, not just reviewers.\n\n- Verified against the live terminal list.\n- Executed in the SAME action block as the merge, never deferred to a future settle.\n- **Ruled:** by the human 2026-08-17 after the twelve-zombie-terminal lapse (orchestrator.md, third lapse) — an action that exists only inside a sent message does not exist.\n- Worktree removal is a SEPARATE step after the merge is confirmed, never bundled into the merge command (cleanup bundled with the merge cannot be interrupted separately — twice today's lesson too: verify the merge landed before removing anything).\n- After the merge is confirmed the orchestrator syncs its own $PWD: `git pull --ff-only`.","after":["dag-pr-merge"],"created":"2026-08-17T19:20:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:05:17-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-a","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1V","title":"review: first reviewer — named from the roster at dispatch","todo":true,"desc":"WHO reviews is never written here: the menu is the roster — `agents-root`'s children in agents.olai (a `ref` the clone's `reviewer` prop takes; the typed gate refuses a name off the roster). The clone's step title takes the chosen reviewer's name (`review: pi (split)`); the template holds only the role (ir-agent-menu, 2026-08-25 — the old steps hardcoded grok/opencode in title AND id while the roster moved on).\n\nTHE STAGE'S LAW (graduated from instructions.md — ir-pipeline-prose, 2026-08-25):\n- The reviewer reviews per HACKING.md in the repo and posts its review as ONE PR comment — verdict + MUST/SHOULD/NIT at file:line.\n- Reviewers READ CODE: no suite runs, no CI, one surgical probe max, never edit/push/merge — the reviewer contract on agents-root is binding; gate verification is the orchestrator's.\n- Never two agents WRITING the same files at once. Reviews are reads — fanning out is safe; writers wait (the edge rule in the root).\n\nSPAWN SHAPE (the charter's rule, enforced by the human 2026-08-16): a reviewer opens as a SPLIT of the author's terminal — kolu create --parent &lt;author-terminal&gt; --cwd &lt;worktree&gt; — never as a top-level terminal.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:19-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:28-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-b","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1l","title":"review: second reviewer — named from the roster at dispatch (skipped when the lane names one)","todo":true,"desc":"Same law and spawn shape as the first review step — the roster names who, the clone's title takes the name, this template holds the role. A lane ruled single-reviewer clones one review step; the open one-vs-N question (whether the template should hold one role step cloned per reviewer instead of two) lives in brainstorming/instructions-breakdown.md.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:38-04:00"}
